{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>You have assigned.</b> She is fitting for him, for she performs deeds of kindness, and worthy to enter the house of Abraham. And the meaning of הֹכַחְתָּ is 'you have chosen' — אפרו״בישט בְּלַעַ״ז." "<b>And by it I shall know.</b> A term of supplication — 'make it known to me through it.'" "<b>That you have shown kindness.</b> If she be of his family and fitting for him — I shall know that you have shown kindness."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "the la'az אפרובישט/אפרובישט corresponds to Old French apercever or aprovéer, 'to discern/approve' — exact Old French form uncertain."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:09.120466437Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}